\details{
The Spanish Basketball Federation (FEB) wrappers cover Primera FEB, Segunda
FEB and Liga Femenina Endesa (plus the federation's other groups on the same
routes). They mirror sdv-py's \code{sportsdataverse.basketball.feb} wrappers of
the same names: same arguments, the same snake_case columns and types, one
row per sdv-py row.

\strong{Legal notice.} The FEB's aviso legal (legal notice) asserts
intellectual-property rights over the site's content and its databases (the
EU database right). It has no explicit scraping clause, and robots.txt
answers 404 on both hosts. Fetching for your own use on your own machine is
how these wrappers are meant to be used; check the notice before you
republish the data.

\strong{Unofficial and unsupported.} The LiveStats API
(\code{intrafeb.feb.es}) is the federation's own widget backend, not a documented
public API. It needs a bearer token, which is public: it is read from the
home page of \code{baloncestoenvivo.feb.es} at run time, kept in memory for the R
session (24 h validity, renewed once on an HTTP 401) and never printed,
logged or written. Requests are spaced at least one second apart per host;
429 and 5xx answers are retried (three attempts).

\strong{Coverage.} The game routes answer from 2020-21 (Liga Femenina Endesa from
its first game; Primera FEB from 2021-03-12, so its earlier 2020-21 games
and every earlier season answer 404). 2020-21 play-by-play is text only. The
schedule pages go back to 1996-97 (\code{season = 1997}).

\strong{Seasons} are END years (\code{season = 2027} is 2026-27); the site's own \code{t}
key is the START year, so the request sends \code{t = season - 1}.

\strong{Errors} are classed conditions, never a warning plus an empty frame:
\code{hoopR_no_data} (HTTP 404, an unknown group, a schedule page with no games,
an empty overview window), \code{hoopR_bad_request} (HTTP 400 / 422, or a
\code{game_id}, \code{group} or \code{season} that is not a non-negative integer) and
\code{hoopR_asset_fetch} (any other failure: another status, a transport error,
a token the API still rejects after one renewal, a non-JSON or non-HTML
body, an error or changed envelope, a play-by-play of another game, a page
for another group or season, or layout drift). All inherit \code{hoopR_error}.
